# Not written:
#   Rule @900.0: not converted: source '$$ Management Servers': an alias, whose value is set per engine, and the input holds no engine; not converted: destination '$$ Local Cluster': an alias, whose value is set per engine, and the input holds no engine; references '$$ Management Servers': an alias, whose value is s
#   internal zone out: the source of the rule is in zone Internal, and a rule of Google Cloud names no zone: give the networks behind Internal with --zone-network
#   not to dmz: not converted: negated destination that does not name the same on both sides of NAT rule 'publish web' (pub-web, 192.168.10.10)
#   updates by name: the destination 'updates.example.com (names)' holds members only its platform knows; a rule of Google Cloud names addresses
#   zone or web host out: the source of the rule is in zone Internal, and a rule of Google Cloud names no zone: give the networks behind Internal with --zone-network; the destination of the rule is in zone External, and a rule of Google Cloud names no zone: give the networks behind External with --zone-network
#   zone or web host out (2): the destination of the rule is in zone External, and a rule of Google Cloud names no zone: give the networks behind External with --zone-network
#   vpn only: not converted: it matches traffic of VPNs only (Source VPN)
#   ping out: what it allows cannot be said by a rule of Google Cloud
#   no social: no port mapping for application(s) Facebook; supply one with --app-map; a service of the rule cannot be read
#   helpdesk to dmz: source user match helpdesk is not converted
#   office web: schedule 'Office hours' is not converted; the rule would apply at all times
#   block list: not converted: it has a block list (it discards what the dynamic block list holds, and lets the rest go on)
#   lan but admins: what it allows cannot be said by a rule of Google Cloud
#   v6 ping: what it allows cannot be said by a rule of Google Cloud

